# mcp-unsupported-version-rejected - a client that consistently declares a
# dropped revision is told which revision to retry with.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-mcp2026-1-stateless-core AC-2. The header and params._meta
# both say 2025-06-18, so this is NOT a header mismatch: it passes header
# validation and _meta parsing and is refused by the version check with HTTP 400
# and JSON-RPC -32022, carrying data.supported and data.requested.
#
# MCP 2026-07-28 basic/versioning: "If the server does not implement the
# requested version ... it MUST respond with an UnsupportedProtocolVersionError
# listing the versions it does support", and the HTTP binding pins the status to
# 400 Bad Request. data.supported is what the client retries against, so it is
# asserted EXACTLY -- a one-element array, closing bracket immediately after --
# rather than with a substring match that a surviving legacy revision would also
# satisfy (ai/rules/compatibility.md: no shim for a dropped revision).
#
# The distinction from -32020 is load-bearing: a client that gets -32022 knows
# to renegotiate, a client that gets -32020 knows to fix its headers, and
# collapsing the two would leave it unable to tell which.
#
# PREVENTS: 2025-06-18, 2025-03-26 or 2024-11-05 quietly remaining in the
# supported set, a version rejection reported as a header mismatch, and a 200
# for a revision this server no longer speaks.

stdin=mcp:terminator=EOF_MCP
# probe-meta drives BOTH the body _meta and the derived MCP-Protocol-Version
# header, so header and body agree and the header guard has nothing to say.
probe-meta protocolVersion 2025-06-18
probe tools/list
# The rejection is per request, not a latch: a conformant call still works.
probe tools/list
EOF_MCP

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze --mcp $PORT -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test mcp --port $PORT:stdin=mcp:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=probe status=400 code=-32022
expect=stdout:contains=unsupported protocol version
expect=stdout:pattern="requested":"2025-06-18"
expect=stdout:pattern="supported":\["2026-07-28"\]
expect=stdout:pattern=(?s)status=400 code=-32022.*probe status=200 code=ok
# A dropped revision must not come back as a header-contract failure.
reject=stdout:contains=code=-32020
